## Why This Is Asked
Tests multi-source timestamp normalization, Parquet partitioning strategies, and foundational data quality practices—core competencies for entry-level data engineers working with real-world SaaS integrations.

## Key Concepts
- Cross-source timestamp normalization to UTC
- AWS Glue ETL jobs and Data Catalog integration
- Parquet file format with date-based partitioning
- Schema evolution via crawler configuration
- Basic data quality validation and testing frameworks

## Code Example
```javascript
function normalizeTimestamp(ts, formats) {
  // Parse multiple timestamp formats
  for (const format of formats) {
    const parsed = moment(ts, format, true);
    if (parsed.isValid()) {
      return parsed.utc().format();
    }
  }
  throw new Error(`Unable to parse timestamp: ${ts}`);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Practical beginner task validating end-to-end ingestion, data quality, and cataloging.

## Key Concepts
- S3 event-driven ETL
- Glue Spark/DynamicFrame validation
- Quarantine routing for bad records
- Parquet partitioning by date
- Glue Data Catalog and Athena access

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo Glue-like JS snippet for validation
function process(batch){
  const valid=[], quarantined=[];
  for (const r of batch){
    if (r.a != null && r.b != null) valid.push(transform(r));
    else quarantined.push({row:r, validation_reason:'missing_required_fields'});
  }
  writeParquet(valid, datePartition);
  writeJson(quarantined, quarantineBucket);
}
```

